<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="182" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Send Email follow-on uses the shared EmailComposer with From, Cc/Bcc, attachments, templates and AI drafting (F-R4-3, D-219)</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (UAT round 4)</phase>
    <gate>after 179 (shares CreateRecordWizard.tsx)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies shared client code (.ts/.tsx) used by several wizards.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>One change reaches eight wizards and their send path; behaviour must stay byte-identical except agreed changes.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with task 179 (CreateRecordWizard.tsx)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>179</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react, fluent-ui, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>The owner found (UAT round 4, F-R4-3) that the create wizards' Send Email step still uses the old email step. Owner D-219: the step must offer what the Send Email dialog offers — a From choice (My mailbox / Spaarke shared mailbox), To, Cc and Bcc, attachments, templates and AI drafting — and the email is sent when the wizard finishes, filed under the new record.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9 and the @spaarke/ui-components wizard framework (CreateRecordWizard, WizardShell).</role>
  <goal>`SendEmailFollowOnStep` renders `EmailComposer` (no Send button: the wizard sends at Finish) with the From row, Cc, Bcc, attachments, template picker and AI draft; at Finish the email is sent through the same route and request builder the composer uses, from the chosen mailbox, with Cc, Bcc and attachments, filed under the created record; the step no longer says "draft"; plain-text bodies keep their line breaks.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Review sections 2.2 and 3; notes/decisions.md D-219. Wrapper: WizardFollowOns/steps/SendEmailFollowOnStep.tsx:136-151. EmailComposer hides the From row when composeOnly (EmailComposer.tsx ~1281 and ~1339: `!props.composeOnly`); sendMode is engine state (~528). Template and AI handlers come from createXrmEmailComposeHandlers (onListEmailTemplates, onDraftWithAi), wired today by DocumentEmailStep.tsx:320-322 and EmailWorkspaceWidget.tsx:218-220. The current Finish path (EntityCreationService.sendEmail, :877-897) sends To/Cc/subject/body only and defaults bodyFormat to HTML.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/steps/SendEmailFollowOnStep.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.types.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DecisionWizard/steps/EmailMessageFields.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/composeOnlyText.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DecisionWizard/steps/EmailMessageFields.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/src/components/DocumentEmailStep.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="179" status="pending">CreateRecordWizard.tsx edits land first</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner directive 2026-11-12, applies to every file this task touches: reuse the existing side-pane lookup (`DataverseLookupField` over `INavigationService.openLookup`) and the existing `EmailComposer`; never re-create either. A third rendering of the lookup pattern is a defect (review section 4 item 6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Every component changed in this task stays in `@spaarke/ui-components` and receives Dataverse access only through injected services (`INavigationService`, `IDataService`, `authenticatedFetch`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every UI change in this task uses Fluent v9 and semantic tokens only; light and dark both fully themed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests added in this task cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner D-219 (2026-11-12, notes/decisions.md) Q2-Q4: From choice, Cc and Bcc, attachments, templates and AI drafting are all ON in this step, matching the Send Email dialog.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Showing the From row in compose-only mode is ONE optional EmailComposer prop (default keeps today's behaviour for every other composeOnly host, e.g. the decision wizard). Do not fork the composer or copy its From menu.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">At Finish, send through the composer's own request building (the same path SendEmailDialog / DocumentEmailStep use) with associations = the created record; do not extend EntityCreationService.sendEmail with a parallel attachment/Bcc implementation. If the composer exposes no reusable request builder, STOP (escalation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Move EmailMessageFields.toPlainText (:45-52) into EmailComposer/composeOnlyText.ts and import it from both places; do not copy it.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/control-initialization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-ui-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-react-version-boundaries.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/wizard-side-pane-lookup-and-email-compose.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Compose-only EmailComposer" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DecisionWizard/steps/EmailMessageFields.tsx">Lines ~54-158: composeOnly, onStateChange into the host state, refuse-fetch test, Cc/Bcc warning.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Composer recipient pane" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts">onLookupRecipients over contact + systemuser (needs the host fetch and BFF base URL the wizards already have).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read notes/decisions.md D-219, review sections 2.2, 3 and 4 items 1, 2 and 4, and how SendEmailDialog and DocumentEmailStep build and send the request.</step>
    <step order="2">Move toPlainText to EmailComposer/composeOnlyText.ts; update EmailMessageFields to import it.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the optional compose-only From prop to EmailComposer (types + render), default off.</step>
    <step order="4">Replace the inner EmailStep in SendEmailFollowOnStep with EmailComposer (composeOnly, From shown, initial values from the follow-on state, onStateChange writing back the full compose state incl. sendMode, Bcc and attachments), template and AI handlers from the host compose handlers, keeping the headerContent slot (Summarize Files toggle).</step>
    <step order="5">At Finish (CreateRecordWizard.tsx ~520-537 and the wizards that send), send via the composer request path with associations = the new record; fix the "draft" wording.</step>
    <step order="6">Add tests and run the dev check.</step>
    <step order="7">Run the tests named in the acceptance criteria, the touched folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and ESLint on touched files in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; all pass.</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record any deviation from this POML, and the dev-check result, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-182-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the composer has no request builder usable after the record exists (only a mounted Send button), STOP and escalate with the options rather than duplicating the send.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a consuming wizard's host cannot supply the compose handlers (no fetch or BFF base URL), STOP and list it.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.tsx ~1281/~1339 hide the From row whenever composeOnly; DecisionWizard/steps/EmailMessageFields.tsx:45-52 holds toPlainText privately.</existing>
    <extension>Yes: one optional prop on the existing composer and one moved helper; no new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the prop the wizard step cannot offer the From choice the owner requires (D-219 Q2); without the shared helper the step must copy toPlainText and the copies drift.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Send Email step matches the Send Email dialog">
      <steps>
        <step>Create Project in the Console on dev, Next steps → Send Email</step>
        <step>Choose From = My mailbox; pick two To recipients and one Bcc with the pane; attach a file; apply a template; use AI draft</step>
        <step>Back, then Next</step>
        <step>Finish</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>From, Cc, Bcc, attachments, template picker and AI draft all present; no Send button; values survive Back/Next; at Finish one email is sent from the chosen mailbox to the To/Cc/Bcc recipients with the attachment, filed under the new project, line breaks intact; dark mode themed.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; in a fresh worktree build ../Spaarke.SdapClient and ../Spaarke.Auth first)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/steps/SendEmailFollowOnStep.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/composeOnlyText.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/steps/__tests__/SendEmailFollowOnStep.composer.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The step renders EmailComposer with no Send button and WITH the From row (My mailbox / Spaarke shared mailbox), Cc, Bcc, attachments, template picker and AI draft.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Other composeOnly hosts (decision wizard) render exactly as today (existing EmailMessageFields tests pass unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Back then Next restores From, To, Cc, Bcc, subject, body and attachments.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The composer makes no network call while composing except template listing and AI draft when the user invokes them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">At Finish the send request carries the chosen sendMode, To, Cc, Bcc, attachments and associations = the created record, built by the composer request path; a send failure is reported and does not undo the record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A plain-text body arrives with its line breaks (bodyFormat PlainText, or the composer's HTML with breaks — whichever the composer path produces; assert the breaks).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The step text no longer says "draft"; SendEmailFollowOnStep no longer imports ../../EmailStep.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Summarize Files wizard's header toggle still renders and works.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: Bcc is never silently dropped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (closed set, every task): no new lookup component, no new email form, no change to the behaviour of the inline `LookupField.tsx`, and no `Xrm` import added to any component file (the host injects `INavigationService`; ADR-012).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched folders pass unchanged unless a criterion above names the change; tsc clean; no new ESLint errors in touched files.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Rewritten 2026-11-12 for D-219 (full composer parity). Source: projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md (Fable review 2026-11-12) and UAT round 4 findings F-R4-2 / F-R4-3 (notes/uat-v4-log.md).</notes>
